-- Playbook ve-pricing-points-passport: Founding Member deadline, no comps, and giving points (Sean, 2026-11-01). Safe to run twice.
insert into public.playbook_records (slug, brand_slug, author, body, source, kind)
select 've-pricing-points-passport', 'vegans-explore', 'Logan', $pb$DECISION AND BUILD RECORD, 2026-11-01 (Sean, Logan). Founding Members, no comps, and giving points.
SEAN'S WORDS. "I'm not going to comp anybody. If anybody doesn't want to sign up, then they miss out on being a founding member." "Your chance of becoming a founding member expires at midnight on January 1st. At that point, you will no longer be able to become a founding member. And that's a thing that sits on your profile." And on John Thomas (TheBodybuildingVegan, johnatbhs@gmail.com, paid the $11 on 2026-11-01 and already gave all 1,125 of his points to two listings): "I want to give John Thomas some points because of all he's contributed to Vegans Explore, and he paid for his membership."
DECIDED. 1. No more comped memberships. Comps already given (Joshua Mattey and the others) stay Founding Members. 2. Anyone who pays the $11 before midnight Eastern on January 1, 2027 (2027-01-01T05:00Z) is a Founding Member for good; after that the $11 is the Passport, no longer a Founding Membership. 3. Sean can give any member points for what they have contributed.
DONE AND LIVE. Migration 20261101_founding_member_deadline.sql applied: ve_site_settings founding_member {deadline, deadline_words, comps false}, ve_founding_deadline(), trigger trg_ve_founding_on_paid on members (sets founding_member when entry_paid_at is first set before the deadline; never on Guide accounts). Found while checking: until now only invitations set founding_member, so paying members were never marked. The backfill marked John Thomas, Ron Arrindell and two internal accounts. The member card already shows the Founding Member tag.
BUILT, NOT DEPLOYED (branch claude/quirky-mendel-4w21bv only, a WIP commit). ve-dashboard give_points (super admin; 1 to 100,000; ve_points_grant reason admin_adjust, ref founder:<uuid>:<note>; refused for super admins and Guide accounts) and member_card gifts (the last 10). Dashboard member card: Give points (quick picks 111, 500, 1,100, 2,500, 5,000; amount; why; confirm; past gifts listed). Not tested, not deployed, center-console not pushed to main.
TO DO NEXT. a. Test and deploy give_points, then Sean gives John Thomas his points (amount is Sean's). b. A way to find any member to open their card (today only Recent Members, votes, leads, the leaderboard and the Inbox open one); John is in Recent Members. c. The deadline in the words: the Passport Guide (passport.html, Overview and Get your Passport), the $11 window in public/ve-auth.js, /policies#membership, the Guides' facts (ve-guide-platform-facts) and a saved answer (When can I become a Founding Member?), the nav announcement (ve_nav_announcements), the dashboard welcome ("Become a Founding Member any time" is now wrong), invitation emails (ve-invites), the Founding Members console. Suggested line: "Founding Membership closes at midnight Eastern on January 1, 2027. Join before then and Founding Member stays on your profile for good." d. Founding Member on the member's own profile and dashboard (the eyebrow reads Founding Member for every active member today; make it read founding_member), and later a badge on their People page and posts. e. No comps in the Depot: take "On us" / "A membership on us" out of Depot > Invites, Founding Members and Ambassadors (or hide it behind the comps setting, false), and decide what an Ambassador invitation is without a comp. f. After January 1: the Passport words drop Founding, the trigger stops by itself.$pb$, 'text', 'decision'
where not exists (select 1 from public.playbook_records where slug = 've-pricing-points-passport' and body like 'DECISION AND BUILD RECORD, 2026-11-01 (Sean, Logan). Founding%');
